config DEMO_MISSING_PAGE
    bool "Hide weather page in demo fixture"
    default n
    help
        Remove the weather page from the deterministic demo registry.

config BATTERY_CALIBRATION_PERMILLE
    int "Battery divider calibration (permille of the nominal 3x divider)"
    default 1000
    help
        Real dividers run a few percent off nominal. 1000 applies no trim.

        With a multimeter: read the reported millivolts (Settings shows them),
        measure across the cell terminals with USB unplugged - charging holds
        the terminal voltage up - and set this to
        1000 * multimeter_mV / reported_mV.

        Without one, a fully charged cell is its own reference. A CC/CV charger
        terminates a single Li-ion cell at 4200 mV, to about a percent, so:
        leave the board on USB until the reported figure stops rising and holds
        steady for an hour or more, then set this to 4200000 / reported_mV.
        Confirm it really has plateaued before trusting it - a cell still
        charging is not at 4200 and would calibrate this the wrong way.

        The ADC itself already uses the chip's factory curve-fitting
        calibration, so this trims the divider ratio only, and the honest
        expectation is a couple of percent rather than precision. That is
        enough for the percentage; it matters most for the overvoltage
        thresholds, which a reading that is low by 3% would never reach.
